{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"oxymoronic-industrial-wrasse","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Problem\nThe scheduled Test Suite (mirror) Windows sweep reports hundreds of setup errors with `AttributeError: 'NoneType' object has no attribute 'flock'`. The suspected path is `src/rebar/_store/git_locking.py`: it explicitly tolerates `import fcntl` failure by setting `fcntl = None`, but later lock acquisition/release call sites invoke `fcntl.flock(...)` unconditionally.\n\n## Plan\n1. Confirm the Windows/no-fcntl contract by inspecting the guarded import, CI sweep matrix, nearby docs/tests, and any existing fallback/no-op/alternative advisory-lock patterns.\n2. Prove the mechanism locally on macOS by simulating Windows with `git_locking.fcntl = None` and driving `_store_git_op_lock` / `fetch_coordination_lock` through tests that fail with the current AttributeError.\n3. If legitimacy is `defect`, preserve Unix behavior exactly and add the smallest no-fcntl-safe branch/fallback consistent with existing precedent.\n4. Add regression coverage for no-fcntl operation and ensure the test has mutation teeth by reintroducing the missing guard in a sandboxed mutation check.\n5. Run targeted tests, then `make lint` and the default suite before Gerrit.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A no-fcntl simulation for `_store_git_op_lock` no longer raises `AttributeError` and still executes the protected operation.\n- [ ] A no-fcntl simulation for `fetch_coordination_lock` no longer raises `AttributeError` and still preserves existing cleanup semantics.\n- [ ] Unix `fcntl.flock` behavior is unchanged and covered by existing tests or a focused assertion.\n- [ ] The RCA comment cites the confirmed mechanism, legitimacy source, caller sweep, sibling sweep, and caused-by attribution.\n- [ ] Gerrit change is submitted only after `LLM-Review +1` and `Verified +1`.","id":"0e7d-ee49-f92b-44c6","parent_id":"","priority":2,"repos":["navapbc/rebar"],"tags":["ci","windows","debugging"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Windows sweep fails when git locking calls fcntl.flock while fcntl is absent"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788217723482211862,"uuid":"1e251037-888c-4a81-93fb-1a8119f64d81"}